  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reducing TB incidence and TB related mortality among Somalis - Somalia (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia, Tuberculosis, World Vision International (WVI Somalia)This program has the following goals: The reduce the TB incidence from 250/100,000 in 2021 to 190/100,000 in 2026.. The objectives of this program are: The goal is to increase TB case notification from the current 17,422 tin 2021 to 26,966 in 2026, and maintain treatment success rate of 90% by end of 2026..  To increase the number of RR/MDR TB cases enrolled on treatment from 345 in 2022 to 1047 in 2026..  To increase the treatment success rate of RR/MDR TB from 78% in the cohort of 2020 to &gt;85% in the cohort of 2024..  To increase number of all diagnosed TB patients are tested for HIV and are aware of their HIV status, and to increase the proportion of TB/HIV coinfected patients on ART from the current 84% to above 90% by 2026.</narrative>
  </description>
